# 🤖 claude-tab-namer

A Claude Code hook that automatically names your terminal tabs based on conversation context. No more guessing which "node" tab is which.

![Before and After](https://img.shields.io/badge/tabs-auto--named-blue)

## Before & After

| Before | After |
|--------|-------|
| `node` · `node` · `node` | `🤖 Site Builder Implementation` · `🤖 Fix Auth Middleware` · `🤖 DB Migration Setup` |

## How It Works

1. Claude Code finishes a response → fires the `Stop` hook
2. The script reads the conversation transcript from the session JSONL file
3. Calls `claude -p` (one-shot prompt mode) with Haiku to generate a 2–5 word title
4. Sets the terminal tab name via an OSC escape sequence

Uses your existing Claude Code auth — no separate API key needed.

## Installation

### 1. Clone the repo

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/claude-tab-namer.git
```

### 2. Copy the hook script

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.claude/hooks
cp claude-tab-namer/tab-namer.sh ~/.claude/hooks/tab-namer.sh
chmod +x ~/.claude/hooks/tab-namer.sh
```

### 3. Register the hook

Add this to `~/.claude/settings.json` (create the file if it doesn't exist, or merge into your existing config):

```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "Stop": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "bash ~/.claude/hooks/tab-namer.sh",
            "timeout": 15000
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

### 4. Configure your IDE terminal

Add this to your Cursor or VS Code `settings.json` (Cmd+Shift+P → "Preferences: Open User Settings (JSON)"):

```json
{
  "terminal.integrated.tabs.title": "${sequence}",
  "terminal.integrated.tabs.enabled": true
}
```

This tells the terminal to respect escape-sequence tab names instead of showing the default process name.

### 5. Restart Claude Code

Open a new terminal, start `claude`, send a message, and wait for the response to complete. Your tab name should update automatically.

## Configuration

Optional environment variables:

| Variable | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `CLAUDE_NAMED_PREFIX` | `🤖` | Emoji/text prefix for tab titles |
| `CLAUDE_NAMED_MODEL` | `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` | Model used for title generation |

## How It Manages Costs

- Generates a title on the **first response** only
- Refreshes every **5 turns** in case the conversation shifts
- Uses **Haiku** (fastest, cheapest model)
- Each title generation costs a fraction of a cent

## Troubleshooting

**Tab still says "node"**
→ Make sure you added `"terminal.integrated.tabs.title": "${sequence}"` to your IDE settings and restarted the terminal.

**Title never generates**
→ Run the hook manually to debug:
```bash
rm -rf ${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/claude-tab-namer/
echo '{"session_id":"test","transcript_path":"PATH_TO_A_SESSION_JSONL","hook_event_name":"Stop"}' \
  | bash -x ~/.claude/hooks/tab-namer.sh
```

**Auth conflict warning**
→ If you see "Both a token and an API key are set", the hook's `claude -p` call uses your existing OAuth login — no `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` needed. You can safely unset it.

